WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.437 --> 00:00:05.003
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:05.003 --> 00:00:07.024
Today, I'm going to talk about
the seven lifestyle changes

00:00:07.024 --> 00:00:10.196
that you need to adopt to be a success.

00:00:10.196 --> 00:00:11.563
And as always guys, if you hear a point

00:00:11.563 --> 00:00:12.679
that really resonates with you,

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.427
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:14.427 --> 00:00:15.832
put quotes around it so other people

00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:18.108
can be inspired as well,
and also writing it down

00:00:18.108 --> 00:00:20.164
helps you lock it in for yourself too.

00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:20.997
Enjoy.

00:00:30.731 --> 00:00:31.564
So I've been asking entrepreneurs

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:32.397
what are the habits that you need

00:00:32.397 --> 00:00:33.451
to have to be a success?

00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:35.063
What do you see in morning routines

00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:37.621
and what do you see in lifestyle
changes that people make

00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:39.415
to go from having a job

00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:42.004
to becoming a successful entrepreneur

00:00:42.004 --> 00:00:43.653
and taking an idea that you have

00:00:43.653 --> 00:00:45.145
and making something amazing?

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.556
What are the changes you
need to make in your life

00:00:46.556 --> 00:00:48.265
to really get there?

00:00:48.265 --> 00:00:50.035
And so today I'm going to share with you

00:00:50.035 --> 00:00:51.600
my seven lifestyle changes that I think

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.767
every entrepreneur needs to
make to become a success.

00:00:58.277 --> 00:01:01.047
Number one is establish a
morning routine for success.

00:01:01.047 --> 00:01:03.433
I think this is so critical, so important.

00:01:03.433 --> 00:01:07.150
Most people wake up, and their
life just explodes on them.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.572
They have a morning routine,

00:01:08.572 --> 00:01:10.062
but it wasn't designed with purpose.

00:01:10.062 --> 00:01:12.653
It's wake up, go to the
washroom, grab a cup of coffee,

00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:14.259
breakfast, and rush out.

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:16.611
It's not designed with
intent and with purpose.

00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:18.265
I think what happens far too often

00:01:18.265 --> 00:01:20.659
is entrepreneurs get inspired by something

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:23.459
at random points in
time, and then they have

00:01:23.459 --> 00:01:25.433
these moments of boldness where they want

00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:28.163
to create something amazing,
and then they wake up

00:01:28.163 --> 00:01:29.764
the next day and it's over.

00:01:29.764 --> 00:01:31.925
They're back to their baseline again.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.575
They fall back down to earth.

00:01:33.575 --> 00:01:36.198
They think about all those
limiting person beliefs,

00:01:36.198 --> 00:01:37.577
and they say that big bold
idea that I had yesterday,

00:01:37.577 --> 00:01:39.327
I can't do that, that's too crazy,

00:01:39.327 --> 00:01:41.587
what was I thinking,
that was really stupid,

00:01:41.587 --> 00:01:42.912
who am I to do that?

00:01:42.912 --> 00:01:43.958
You're falling back down.

00:01:43.958 --> 00:01:46.214
You're living a limited
life all over again,

00:01:46.214 --> 00:01:48.330
and it happens to you every single day.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.216
And so whatever that thing
was that got you inspired,

00:01:51.216 --> 00:01:54.353
motivated, thinking big,
resourceful, unstoppable ...

00:01:54.353 --> 00:01:56.907
Instead of it happening
randomly once a week

00:01:56.907 --> 00:01:59.273
or once a month or whenever it happens,

00:01:59.273 --> 00:02:01.383
schedule it in within
intent, with purpose.

00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:03.250
Put it into your morning routine

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.488
so that every day you
start with that thing

00:02:05.488 --> 00:02:07.653
that gets you feeling big,
bold, brave, and unstoppable.

00:02:07.653 --> 00:02:09.262
Put that into your morning routine

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.872
and then let it carry forward for you

00:02:10.872 --> 00:02:12.872
for the rest of the day.

00:02:15.686 --> 00:02:19.526
Lifestyle change number two is
create a better environment.

00:02:19.526 --> 00:02:20.964
The environment that you're in matters.

00:02:20.964 --> 00:02:22.820
The people that you're around matters.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.923
The physical environment
that you're in matters.

00:02:24.923 --> 00:02:26.735
The sounds that are happening matter.

00:02:26.735 --> 00:02:30.128
And so when you're working
or when you're in work mode,

00:02:30.128 --> 00:02:31.607
what are you listening to?

00:02:31.607 --> 00:02:33.579
What sounds are coming out?

00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:35.058
What's on your walls around you?

00:02:35.058 --> 00:02:37.088
Are you in an environment
that makes you come alive,

00:02:37.088 --> 00:02:38.524
that makes you want to think bigger?

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.511
When I'm at my office,
I have these posters

00:02:40.511 --> 00:02:42.280
on the wall of people who inspire me

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.556
for different reasons.

00:02:43.556 --> 00:02:44.803
Five different people who inspire me

00:02:44.803 --> 00:02:46.369
for different messages
and different reasons.

00:02:46.369 --> 00:02:48.847
I walk into there and I'm like this is it.

00:02:48.847 --> 00:02:50.849
I got to do something big today.

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:52.336
And those five people
may mean nothing to you.

00:02:52.336 --> 00:02:54.403
That's okay.
It means something to me.

00:02:54.403 --> 00:02:56.177
It helps me believe more.

00:02:56.177 --> 00:02:58.401
And so creating that physical
environment for yourself.

00:02:58.401 --> 00:03:00.013
A lot of people will say
well I don't have the money

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:03.444
to have a private island,
because the private island

00:03:03.444 --> 00:03:05.387
is going to be the thing
that makes me come alive.

00:03:05.387 --> 00:03:07.464
You can have a picture
of a private island.

00:03:07.464 --> 00:03:08.406
You can get the feeling
of a private island.

00:03:08.406 --> 00:03:10.469
It doesn't have to cost a lot of money

00:03:10.469 --> 00:03:13.646
to create an amazing
environment for yourself.

00:03:13.646 --> 00:03:15.578
Think about the friends that
you're hanging around with.

00:03:15.578 --> 00:03:17.475
Thinking about the videos that you watch

00:03:17.475 --> 00:03:18.915
and the things that you consume.

00:03:18.915 --> 00:03:22.287
Are you going on YouTube
and watching prank videos,

00:03:22.287 --> 00:03:24.796
or are you going on YouTube
and watching videos like this

00:03:24.796 --> 00:03:26.735
where you get to be motivated, inspired,

00:03:26.735 --> 00:03:28.173
and learn something?

00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:30.154
Having that built in so that
you have a great environment

00:03:30.154 --> 00:03:31.592
that sets you up for success

00:03:31.592 --> 00:03:34.469
and reinforces the success all the time.

00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:35.955
It's hard when you're an entrepreneur

00:03:35.955 --> 00:03:37.272
because we don't have a boss.

00:03:37.272 --> 00:03:40.108
There's nobody saying why are
you on Facebook right now?

00:03:40.108 --> 00:03:43.222
There's nobody's saying why
are you answering those Snaps

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.201
and on Instagram and just texting people?

00:03:45.201 --> 00:03:46.682
Why are you not working?

00:03:46.682 --> 00:03:47.761
That's what a boss would do.

00:03:47.761 --> 00:03:49.168
We are our own boss.

00:03:49.168 --> 00:03:50.827
And there's a great freedom in that.

00:03:50.827 --> 00:03:52.351
There's an amazing freedom.

00:03:52.351 --> 00:03:53.964
That's part of the reason
why maybe you wanted to start

00:03:53.964 --> 00:03:55.982
your own business, but there's also a lack

00:03:55.982 --> 00:03:58.393
of accountability, and so you
want to have an environment

00:03:58.393 --> 00:04:00.105
that holds you accountable.

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:04.250
When I'm working, and I
look up and I see Steve Jobs

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.682
looking back at me, it's
like get back to work Evan,

00:04:06.682 --> 00:04:09.052
keep working, hustle, hustle harder, go.

00:04:09.052 --> 00:04:11.836
When I'm watching videos
and doing the research

00:04:11.836 --> 00:04:12.912
for the videos on this channel,

00:04:12.912 --> 00:04:15.795
it reinforces it, like all
these successful people

00:04:15.795 --> 00:04:17.809
are telling me every day,
you got to work harder,

00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:19.701
you got to push better,
you got to learn more.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:22.507
It just inspires me to want to
keep doing my absolute best,

00:04:22.507 --> 00:04:24.899
and they hold me accountable.

00:04:24.899 --> 00:04:26.426
My environment holds me accountable

00:04:26.426 --> 00:04:29.066
because I don't have
a boss in my business.

00:04:29.066 --> 00:04:31.112
So you have to create an environment

00:04:31.112 --> 00:04:33.945
that is designed for your success.

00:04:35.172 --> 00:04:37.570
Lifestyle change number three to adopt

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.596
is you need to accept responsibility.

00:04:39.596 --> 00:04:43.394
Stop complaining and start
accepting responsibility.

00:04:43.394 --> 00:04:45.621
A lot of people use excuses
for why their business

00:04:45.621 --> 00:04:46.863
is not successful, right?

00:04:46.863 --> 00:04:47.912
The economy's in the tank.

00:04:47.912 --> 00:04:49.724
We have the new president.

00:04:49.724 --> 00:04:51.711
Interest rates are up or
interest rates are down.

00:04:51.711 --> 00:04:53.308
Or there's a war, whatever.

00:04:53.308 --> 00:04:54.804
There's always an excuse.

00:04:54.804 --> 00:04:55.664
There's always a reason why.

00:04:55.664 --> 00:04:58.069
And as long as you can
blame somebody else,

00:04:58.069 --> 00:04:59.389
you are never going to do anything.

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:01.341
As long as you can put
the blame over here,

00:05:01.341 --> 00:05:04.176
it's the president's fault
that I'm not more successful,

00:05:04.176 --> 00:05:05.749
that means you don't have to do anything,

00:05:05.749 --> 00:05:07.977
because you gave up the responsibility.

00:05:07.977 --> 00:05:09.298
It's their fault.

00:05:09.298 --> 00:05:12.317
Successful entrepreneurs,
successful people,

00:05:12.317 --> 00:05:14.226
accept the responsibility.

00:05:14.226 --> 00:05:17.190
If you lost a customer, it's your fault.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.442
If you're not more
successful, it's your fault.

00:05:20.442 --> 00:05:23.572
Always accept responsibility
in every situation.

00:05:23.572 --> 00:05:25.343
Your relationship isn't
where you want to go?

00:05:25.343 --> 00:05:27.986
It's not your partner's fault,
it's your fault, fix it, now.

00:05:27.986 --> 00:05:30.617
Sure, are other people involved?

00:05:30.617 --> 00:05:34.200
Yes, but blaming them
doesn't fix anything.

00:05:35.733 --> 00:05:39.048
So accepting responsibility
in every situation,

00:05:39.048 --> 00:05:41.903
understanding how do I
fix this, what can I do?

00:05:41.903 --> 00:05:43.798
Because I can't control everything else.

00:05:43.798 --> 00:05:45.592
I'm not controlling interest rates.

00:05:45.592 --> 00:05:47.085
I'm not controlling the economy.

00:05:47.085 --> 00:05:48.855
I control what I do every day.

00:05:48.855 --> 00:05:50.635
So let's fix that.

00:05:50.635 --> 00:05:52.567
If you're not where you
want to be, it's your fault.

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:55.655
Accept that, and start
making some changes.

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:57.337
It sucks, because it's depressing,

00:05:57.337 --> 00:05:59.206
because it's so easy to
have somebody to blame,

00:05:59.206 --> 00:06:01.252
but it's also empowering because you know

00:06:01.252 --> 00:06:02.572
that if you start making some changes,

00:06:02.572 --> 00:06:04.950
you can start seeing big
things happen for you.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:07.183
A lot of the best opportunities
come from complaints.

00:06:07.183 --> 00:06:08.706
Where other people are complaining

00:06:08.706 --> 00:06:11.026
that something is a certain way,

00:06:11.026 --> 00:06:14.651
successful entrepreneurs turn
that into an opportunity.

00:06:14.651 --> 00:06:16.260
The fact that people are complaining

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:17.591
means there's a pain.

00:06:17.591 --> 00:06:19.043
Take that pain and solve it.

00:06:19.043 --> 00:06:20.488
Here's a business for you.

00:06:20.488 --> 00:06:22.180
And what's what successful people do.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.404
They don't complain.
They don't wine.

00:06:24.404 --> 00:06:25.809
They don't just talk to their friends

00:06:25.809 --> 00:06:27.252
and say how bad everything is.

00:06:27.252 --> 00:06:29.648
They accept responsibility,
they take action,

00:06:29.648 --> 00:06:33.815
and they turn those pain
points into opportunities.

00:06:36.524 --> 00:06:39.081
Lifestyle change number four
is you need to take action.

00:06:39.081 --> 00:06:42.954
Take action.
Successful people take action.

00:06:42.954 --> 00:06:45.845
Too many people just want to be a success.

00:06:45.845 --> 00:06:48.076
They get off just thinking
about ideas, right?

00:06:48.076 --> 00:06:49.520
Here's another idea.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:50.754
Oh it'd be great if I could do this.

00:06:50.754 --> 00:06:52.403
Or hey, here's what I would
do if I owned McDonalds.

00:06:52.403 --> 00:06:54.760
That's great, but nothing's
ever going to happen for you

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.037
until you take action.

00:06:56.037 --> 00:06:57.503
Thinking alone is not enough.

00:06:57.503 --> 00:06:58.940
Thinking alone is only
part of the equation.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.057
You got to do something about it.

00:07:00.057 --> 00:07:02.351
And what happens a lot if you get an idea.

00:07:02.351 --> 00:07:03.816
This happens to a lot of people.

00:07:03.816 --> 00:07:05.291
You get some idea, and you have your job.

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:07.549
But you don't do anything about that idea.

00:07:07.549 --> 00:07:09.214
You just have some job,
you keep going on it

00:07:09.214 --> 00:07:10.755
because you say all these
reasons why you can't

00:07:10.755 --> 00:07:13.388
do this business, and so
you're working on this job,

00:07:13.388 --> 00:07:16.197
and then somebody else
goes off and makes millions

00:07:16.197 --> 00:07:18.488
of dollars and has a
huge impact on the world,

00:07:18.488 --> 00:07:19.996
off of that idea.
You say, that was my idea.

00:07:19.996 --> 00:07:22.312
No it wasn't.
That was their idea too.

00:07:22.312 --> 00:07:25.278
The only difference is they
did something about it.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:28.161
So don't be upset at them.
Be upset at yourself.

00:07:28.161 --> 00:07:30.054
It's nobody's fault.
Take responsibility.

00:07:30.054 --> 00:07:32.564
Nobody else's fault but your own.

00:07:32.564 --> 00:07:34.130
You have to do something.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.568
Having the idea is not enough.

00:07:36.568 --> 00:07:38.545
Have a big vision, it's
amazing, it's great,

00:07:38.545 --> 00:07:39.586
I want you to have that big vision,

00:07:39.586 --> 00:07:41.744
take an action step, small.

00:07:41.744 --> 00:07:44.513
Think big, act small,
consistently, every day.

00:07:44.513 --> 00:07:48.395
Go, do something.
Successful people take action.

00:07:48.395 --> 00:07:50.801
And so the next time you get an idea,

00:07:50.801 --> 00:07:54.559
just find some small way
to start, test it out.

00:07:54.559 --> 00:07:57.537
You may think, hey, it could
be a new lifestyle thing too.

00:07:57.537 --> 00:07:58.902
Hey, I want to take salsa classes.

00:07:58.902 --> 00:08:01.399
Instead of dreaming for years
about taking salsa classes,

00:08:01.399 --> 00:08:05.540
go out and take a salsa class.
You may hate it.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.024
I don't think you'll hate it

00:08:07.024 --> 00:08:08.709
if you take it at (mumbles) Salsa,

00:08:08.709 --> 00:08:10.359
but you may hate it, and
at least now you know.

00:08:10.359 --> 00:08:12.213
You don't have to spend
the rest of your life

00:08:12.213 --> 00:08:14.154
wondering and worrying about it.

00:08:14.154 --> 00:08:15.698
Or you may take it and love it.

00:08:15.698 --> 00:08:17.308
And then you adjust and find other ways

00:08:17.308 --> 00:08:19.036
to get involved in it
and continue dancing.

00:08:19.036 --> 00:08:21.093
Maybe it becomes a business for you.

00:08:21.093 --> 00:08:22.868
When you get an idea about something,

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:25.265
find a small way to get
started immediately.

00:08:25.265 --> 00:08:28.598
Stop waiting, stop delaying.
Take action.

00:08:33.944 --> 00:08:37.156
Now you can't do everything
yourself in your business,

00:08:37.156 --> 00:08:39.669
and you're likely doing things
that you shouldn't be doing.

00:08:39.669 --> 00:08:40.946
If you're doing something important,

00:08:40.946 --> 00:08:42.760
you have to build a team.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.497
The first person I hired
was for one hour a day,

00:08:44.497 --> 00:08:46.674
and he freed up more than
an hour of my time a day

00:08:46.674 --> 00:08:49.879
because he was better
at the work than I was,

00:08:49.879 --> 00:08:51.898
and then I slowly built up my team.

00:08:51.898 --> 00:08:54.246
And so you can hire somebody.

00:08:54.246 --> 00:08:56.639
You may not have enough
money to have somebody

00:08:56.639 --> 00:08:58.032
come on full time on your business,

00:08:58.032 --> 00:08:59.685
but to hire somebody for an hour a day

00:08:59.685 --> 00:09:01.716
or a couple hours a week, to help take off

00:09:01.716 --> 00:09:03.559
some of the tasks that
you shouldn't be doing,

00:09:03.559 --> 00:09:05.300
will really help.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.609
You want to spend as much time
in the CEO role as possible.

00:09:07.609 --> 00:09:08.970
That's where you want to be.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.346
And so looking at your schedule

00:09:10.346 --> 00:09:11.870
and seeing where am I spending time

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:15.076
that should be eliminated?
What things can be automated?

00:09:15.076 --> 00:09:16.238
And then whatever's left
that still has to get done,

00:09:16.238 --> 00:09:18.420
how do I delegate some
of these other things

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:21.231
so that I can focus on what I'm great at.

00:09:21.231 --> 00:09:22.869
So when I started my YouTube channel,

00:09:22.869 --> 00:09:24.241
I did everything myself.

00:09:24.241 --> 00:09:25.680
I'm a big advocate of not spending money

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:26.923
until you're making money.

00:09:26.923 --> 00:09:28.036
No point in hiring somebody

00:09:28.036 --> 00:09:29.525
if you're making zero on your business,

00:09:29.525 --> 00:09:30.930
but as soon as I started making money

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:33.075
on my YouTube channel,
I was doing everything.

00:09:33.075 --> 00:09:34.925
I was the cameraman, I was the
editor, I was the researcher,

00:09:34.925 --> 00:09:36.701
I was in front of the camera, everything.

00:09:36.701 --> 00:09:37.911
As soon as I started making some money

00:09:37.911 --> 00:09:39.792
on my YouTube channel, it put it back in,

00:09:39.792 --> 00:09:42.212
and the first person
I hired was an editor.

00:09:42.212 --> 00:09:43.939
Because editing took me a long time,

00:09:43.939 --> 00:09:45.216
I wasn't very good at it,

00:09:45.216 --> 00:09:46.829
I didn't want to get good
at it, more importantly,

00:09:46.829 --> 00:09:48.829
and then as I started making more,

00:09:48.829 --> 00:09:51.943
I hired more people, more
editors, a cameraman,

00:09:51.943 --> 00:09:56.093
I bought more gear, I got
cameras, I got microphones,

00:09:56.093 --> 00:09:58.524
I got researchers, I got people to help me

00:09:58.524 --> 00:10:00.094
on the YouTube channel with the comments,

00:10:00.094 --> 00:10:02.484
and so my team grew as my business grew,

00:10:02.484 --> 00:10:05.073
but the thing that really helped skyrocket

00:10:05.073 --> 00:10:07.300
the early growth was
getting my first editor.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.412
So as soon as you can afford it,

00:10:08.412 --> 00:10:10.931
bringing somebody on to help
alleviate some of the tasks

00:10:10.931 --> 00:10:12.867
that you're not good at,
and more importantly,

00:10:12.867 --> 00:10:14.975
don't want to get good at either,

00:10:14.975 --> 00:10:17.534
can really help you quickly
scale up your business

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:19.636
and reduce the stress because
you get most stressed out

00:10:19.636 --> 00:10:23.719
when you're doing work
that you don't want to do.

00:10:26.397 --> 00:10:27.774
The number six lifestyle
change you need to make

00:10:27.774 --> 00:10:30.119
to be successful is you
need to be consistent.

00:10:30.119 --> 00:10:32.373
So many people are not consistent.

00:10:32.373 --> 00:10:34.917
So many entrepreneurs I talk to have a day

00:10:34.917 --> 00:10:36.512
where they're on fire
and doing so much work

00:10:36.512 --> 00:10:39.485
and building up and sending
emails and marketing

00:10:39.485 --> 00:10:41.892
and pouring their love
into product development

00:10:41.892 --> 00:10:45.290
and then nothing, the next day nothing,

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.469
the next day nothing,
and it just falls apart,

00:10:47.469 --> 00:10:48.788
until like next week or next month.

00:10:48.788 --> 00:10:50.639
Another great day, super productive.

00:10:50.639 --> 00:10:52.129
You have to understand.

00:10:52.129 --> 00:10:54.815
It takes time for momentum to build.

00:10:54.815 --> 00:10:57.415
You will not have success by
just having these short spurts

00:10:57.415 --> 00:10:59.504
with long gaps in between.

00:10:59.504 --> 00:11:02.857
It's far better to spend
half an hour to an hour

00:11:02.857 --> 00:11:04.503
every single day on your business

00:11:04.503 --> 00:11:07.850
than one day a week all in on the company.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.237
Because momentum takes time to build up.

00:11:10.237 --> 00:11:13.119
If you look at anybody whose
had success in any field.

00:11:13.119 --> 00:11:14.770
Not just entrepreneurship, in any field.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.513
It's not just working.

00:11:16.513 --> 00:11:18.579
It's not just taking action.

00:11:18.579 --> 00:11:22.454
It's taking action
consistently, every single day.

00:11:22.454 --> 00:11:25.865
Put it in your calendar and
sticking by the calendar.

00:11:25.865 --> 00:11:27.847
Doing the work consistently

00:11:27.847 --> 00:11:31.946
is what separates the high
achievers from everybody else.

00:11:31.946 --> 00:11:33.816
And there's always an excuse
for why you can't do it.

00:11:33.816 --> 00:11:35.857
I get it, there's always
some kind of excuse.

00:11:35.857 --> 00:11:37.907
There's a wedding to go to.

00:11:37.907 --> 00:11:39.773
There's an illness in the family.

00:11:39.773 --> 00:11:41.366
There's legit reasons.

00:11:41.366 --> 00:11:42.700
And there's others that are not legit

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.383
that are just based off of your fear.

00:11:45.383 --> 00:11:47.126
You can always find a reason

00:11:47.126 --> 00:11:49.017
why you shouldn't do something, always.

00:11:49.017 --> 00:11:51.367
And if you look at the most
successful people in the world,

00:11:51.367 --> 00:11:55.048
they had more reasons than
you do for not doing anything.

00:11:55.048 --> 00:11:57.351
Look at how they started.
Look at where they came form.

00:11:57.351 --> 00:11:58.795
Most of these people ...

00:11:58.795 --> 00:11:59.865
I'm not talking about inherited wealth.

00:11:59.865 --> 00:12:01.593
I'm talking about people who
built something for themselves.

00:12:01.593 --> 00:12:03.661
Look at where they came from.

00:12:03.661 --> 00:12:06.016
They had less than what
you already have right now.

00:12:06.016 --> 00:12:07.664
They had every excuse in the world

00:12:07.664 --> 00:12:09.025
not to take action consistently.

00:12:09.025 --> 00:12:11.267
Every reason in the world
why they had to go off

00:12:11.267 --> 00:12:12.843
and do something else instead,

00:12:12.843 --> 00:12:14.529
and they found the time, somehow,

00:12:14.529 --> 00:12:16.514
to focus on building this thing

00:12:16.514 --> 00:12:18.873
that they said was important
to them and they did it.

00:12:18.873 --> 00:12:20.524
Meanwhile, you're sitting on your excuses

00:12:20.524 --> 00:12:22.547
and your reasons for why you can't do it.

00:12:22.547 --> 00:12:23.823
Stop the excuses.

00:12:23.823 --> 00:12:26.490
Consistent daily massive action.

00:12:33.003 --> 00:12:35.082
Habit number seven is you
have to believe in yourself.

00:12:35.082 --> 00:12:37.193
I think of all the ones
we've talked about today,

00:12:37.193 --> 00:12:40.484
none of them matter if you
don't believe in yourself.

00:12:40.484 --> 00:12:41.884
You can take lots of action,

00:12:41.884 --> 00:12:43.664
but if you don't believe in
the work that you're doing

00:12:43.664 --> 00:12:45.110
and believe that you can make it happen,

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.010
it's not going to happen.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:49.965
What you believe you can do, you will do.

00:12:49.965 --> 00:12:51.527
If you believe that you can, you can.

00:12:51.527 --> 00:12:55.279
If you believe that you
can't, then you can't.

00:12:55.279 --> 00:12:57.432
So I think one of the most
important things that you can do

00:12:57.432 --> 00:13:01.643
is learn how to develop that
inner belief in yourself.

00:13:01.643 --> 00:13:03.692
I got it a lot through my parents

00:13:03.692 --> 00:13:06.089
who told me I was Evan
Castrilli Carmichael

00:13:06.089 --> 00:13:07.323
and could do anything that I wanted.

00:13:07.323 --> 00:13:08.619
I continue that tradition off to my son

00:13:08.619 --> 00:13:10.993
where every time I drop him off at school

00:13:10.993 --> 00:13:12.744
or say good night,

00:13:12.744 --> 00:13:14.740
it's either Carmichaels can do anything

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:18.168
or I am Haden Carmichael
and I can do anything,

00:13:18.168 --> 00:13:19.676
to give him the confidence in himself,

00:13:19.676 --> 00:13:21.546
but if you don't get that your parents,

00:13:21.546 --> 00:13:23.348
you don't get that from your friends,

00:13:23.348 --> 00:13:25.122
it's fine, get them from videos,

00:13:25.122 --> 00:13:26.592
get them from books,
get them from resources,

00:13:26.592 --> 00:13:27.926
get them from circles around you.

00:13:27.926 --> 00:13:29.652
I got more of my confidence now ongoing

00:13:29.652 --> 00:13:31.174
through the videos that I put up.

00:13:31.174 --> 00:13:33.523
I'm surrounding by
successful people daily.

00:13:33.523 --> 00:13:36.365
Not in person, but through my videos.

00:13:36.365 --> 00:13:38.338
Every day I'm surrounded by Elon Musk.

00:13:38.338 --> 00:13:39.730
and Steve Jobs and Howard Schultz

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:42.325
and all these people
feeding knowledge and wisdom

00:13:42.325 --> 00:13:44.848
and motivation into me,
making me a better leader,

00:13:44.848 --> 00:13:46.327
making me more confident.

00:13:46.327 --> 00:13:50.155
Making me believe in what
I'm doing and in myself more.

00:13:50.155 --> 00:13:50.988
If you want the change the world,

00:13:50.988 --> 00:13:52.838
then you have to believe that
you can change the world.

00:13:52.838 --> 00:13:54.737
You can say it all you want,

00:13:54.737 --> 00:13:56.768
but if you don't believe it,
nothing's going to happen.

00:13:56.768 --> 00:13:59.711
And so building that self confidence up.

00:13:59.711 --> 00:14:01.988
Creating that environment
and that morning routine

00:14:01.988 --> 00:14:04.453
and those rituals, where
if you find the things,

00:14:04.453 --> 00:14:06.845
if this channel makes you
believe in yourself more,

00:14:06.845 --> 00:14:08.527
then watch the channel more.

00:14:08.527 --> 00:14:11.630
If my channel doesn't
do that, unsubscribe,

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:13.399
go somewhere else, but do something.

00:14:13.399 --> 00:14:16.546
Because that inner belief is critical.

00:14:16.546 --> 00:14:18.910
Successful people believe in themselves.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:21.056
Successful people believe
in the vision that they have

00:14:21.056 --> 00:14:22.999
when nobody else believe in it.

00:14:22.999 --> 00:14:25.416
They have this big vision for
what they want to accomplish,

00:14:25.416 --> 00:14:26.660
and everybody thinks they're crazy.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:27.798
It doesn't matter.

00:14:27.798 --> 00:14:29.239
I'm still going to go out and do it.

00:14:29.239 --> 00:14:31.296
You need to have that unshakable belief

00:14:31.296 --> 00:14:33.456
in yourself, in the
project, in the mission,

00:14:33.456 --> 00:14:36.673
if you want to go out sand
make something big happen.

00:14:36.673 --> 00:14:38.571
So that's my take on the
seven lifestyle changes

00:14:38.571 --> 00:14:40.586
that you need to make in
order to be a success.

00:14:40.586 --> 00:14:42.691
I'd love to know what did you guys think.

00:14:42.691 --> 00:14:44.621
Which one was your favorite and why.

00:14:44.621 --> 00:14:46.024
Did I miss an eight, nine, 10,

00:14:46.024 --> 00:14:47.552
that you guys want to add to the list?

00:14:47.552 --> 00:14:48.995
Put it down in the comments below.

00:14:48.995 --> 00:14:50.687
Super curious to hear
what you have to say.

00:14:50.687 --> 00:14:52.424
I also want to give a big
shout out to Katie Kruse.

00:14:52.424 --> 00:14:54.244
Katie, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:14:54.244 --> 00:14:56.679
of my book, Your One Word, and
for making that awesome video

00:14:56.679 --> 00:14:58.522
on it as well.

00:14:58.522 --> 00:15:00.218
I really really really
appreciate the support,

00:15:00.218 --> 00:15:02.074
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed the book.

00:15:02.074 --> 00:15:03.829
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:03.829 --> 00:15:04.662
I believe in you.

00:15:04.662 --> 00:15:06.775
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:15:06.775 --> 00:15:08.313
and whatever your one word is.

00:15:08.313 --> 00:15:10.646
Much love.
I'll see you soon.

